[release] id: soaks:plan-duration
[release] status: failed
[release] at: 2026-08-10
[release] reason: invalidated by the soak isolation rule

The 2026-07-20 `soaks:plan-duration` record was written before the soak
isolation rule existed. It carries no branch, no revision, and no application
digest, so the run it describes cannot be attributed to any tree and cannot
support G1. No `soak:*` pass record ever followed it, and every RQ row in
STATUS-SOFTWARE remains open, so no plan-duration soak completed.

This record supersedes it as failed so `release:status` stops treating the S2
soak wait as started. Restart under the guard:

  git switch -c release/v1.0.0
  npm run release:start-soaks

The relaunch records branch, revision, and application digest, and fails the
run if application code changes while it is in flight.
